---
title: "Figure 1 — AgentCore Gateway Fine-Grained Access Control Sequence Diagram"
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    participant U as Ravi<br/>(Line Supervisor)
    participant C as Amazon Cognito
    participant A as Agent<br/>(Strands SDK)
    participant GW as AgentCore<br/>Gateway
    participant CE as Cedar Policy<br/>Engine
    participant T as MCP Tool<br/>(Lambda)

    %% === Authentication Phase ===
    rect rgb(240, 248, 255)
        Note over U, C: Authentication Phase
        U->>C: Login (credentials)
        C-->>U: JWT {role: line_supervisor, line_scope: Line 7, plant_scope: Plant 2}
        Note over C: JWT Claims:<br/>role = line_supervisor<br/>line_scope = Line 7<br/>plant_scope = Plant 2<br/>equipment_scope = (all within plant)
    end

    %% === Query & Tool Invocation ===
    rect rgb(255, 253, 240)
        Note over U, A: Tool Invocation
        U->>A: "What is the OEE for Line 7?"
        Note right of A: LLM reasons:<br/>Need get_oee_trends(line="Line 7")
        A->>GW: MCP call: get_oee_trends(line="Line 7") + Bearer JWT
    end

    %% === Enrichment Phase ===
    rect rgb(232, 245, 233)
        Note over GW, GW: Enrichment (REQUEST Interceptor)
        Note right of GW: 1. Decode JWT payload<br/>2. Extract role + line_scope<br/>3. Inject user_context into args
    end

    %% === Authorization Phase ===
    rect rgb(243, 229, 245)
        Note over GW, CE: Authorization (Cedar)
        GW->>CE: Evaluate: role=line_supervisor, action=get_oee_trends, line="Line 7"
        Note right of CE: Cedar Evaluation:<br/>permit_all → PERMIT<br/>forbid_line_scope:<br/>"Line 7" in ["Line 7"]? YES<br/>→ No forbid triggered
    end

    %% === ALT: ALLOW vs DENY ===
    alt ALLOW — parameter in user scope
        CE-->>GW: Decision: ALLOW ✓
        GW->>T: Execute Lambda tool target
        activate T
        T-->>GW: OEE data (Line 7, 4 weeks)
        deactivate T
        GW-->>A: Tool result (data)
        A-->>U: "Line 7 OEE is 91.2%, trending up from 87%..."

    else DENY — parameter outside user scope (e.g., Line 4)
        CE-->>GW: Decision: DENY ✗ — "Line 4 not in scope"
        Note over T: MCP Server<br/>NEVER INVOKED
        GW-->>A: Error: "[Policy] Access denied. Scope: Line 7 only"
        Note over A: LLM synthesizes:<br/>ALLOW → data summary<br/>DENY → explains scope + suggests alternative
        A-->>U: "I can't access Line 4 data. Your scope covers Line 7.<br/>Would you like Line 7 OEE instead?"
    end
